## 3. Blocking licenses (require sign-off before any port)

> These licenses are *incompatible* with a proprietary SaaS distribution
> model unless explicitly approved by the consumer's legal team.

| License | Why blocking | Affected dep(s) | Required action |
|---|---|---|---|
| AGPL-3.0 | Network copyleft — SaaS must open source | `<dep>` | Replace or wrap; NO source-port |
| SSPL | Server Side Public License — equivalent to AGPL | `<dep>` | Replace or extract-pattern only |
| GPL-2.0/3.0 | Viral copyleft — would force the consumer to GPL | `<dep>` | Reference only; NEVER source-port |
| Proprietary | Requires commercial agreement | `<dep>` | Anderson sign-off per dep |
| BSL with non-commercial clause | Blocks commercial use | `<dep>` | Verify clause, replace if needed |
| Unknown / missing SPDX | Cannot audit | `<dep>` | Identify license before port |

### 3.1 Decision per blocking dep

For each blocking dep, capture:

- `<dep-name>` — **DECISION**: `replace | wrap | reference-only | approved-by-anderson-on-YYYY-MM-DD`
- Rationale: `<1-3 sentences>`
- Replacement candidate: `<dep-name>` under `<license>` if `replace`

